  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>MnBr</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is a tetrahedral complex. The electronic configuration&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup></math>&nbsp;and it has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;unpaired electrons.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>35</mn></msqrt><mtext>&#160;B.&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>CoF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is an octahedral complex and it is high spin&nbsp;complex. The electronic configuration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><msup><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, it has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;unpaired electrons</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>24</mn></msqrt><mtext>&#160;B.M.&#160;</mtext></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Mn</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is an octahedral complex and it is low spin complex. The electronic configuration&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup></math>&nbsp;it has two&nbsp;unpaired electrons</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>8</mn></msqrt><mtext>&#160;B.M&#160;</mtext></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub><msup><mo>]</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is an octahedral complex and it is low spin complex. The electronic configuration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>eg</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and it has one&nbsp;unpaired electron.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mtext>&#160;B.M&#160;</mtext></math></p><p>Hence the correct answer is option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
